--- !u!114 &4107201604222453752
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4107201604222453508}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 00fda604ac3af404a8e8a7571f24c19d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  allNames:
  - splenius colli muscle
  - musculus splenius colli
  - "muscle spl\xE9nius du cou"
  - "m\xFAsculo splenius colli"
  - "m\xFAsculo espl\xEAnio do pesco\xE7o"
  - muscolo splenius colli
  - splenius colli-spier
  - splenius-colli-muskel
  - "mi\u0119sie\u0144 splenius colli"
  - "\u813E\u9838\u808C\u8089"
  description: "SPLENIUS COLLI/CERVICIS MUSCLE\r\n\r\n\r\nThe splenius cervicis (also
    known as the splenius colli) is a muscle in the back of the neck. \r\n\r\nIt
    arises by a narrow tendinous band from the spinous processes of the third to
    the sixth thoracic vertebrae; it is inserted, by tendinous fasciculi, into the
    posterior tubercles of the transverse processes of the upper two or three cervical
    vertebrae.\r\n\r\nIts name is based on the Greek word \u03C3\u03C0\u03BB\u03B7\u03BD\u03AF\u03BF\u03BD,
    splenion (meaning a bandage) and the Latin word cervix (meaning a neck). \r\n\r\nThe
    word collum also refers to the neck in Latin.The function of the splenius cervicis
    muscle is extension of the cervical spine, rotation to the ipsilateral side and
    lateral flexion to the ipsilateral side.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splenius_cervicis_muscle\r\n;;;ES;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULO
    ESPLENIUS COLLI/CERVICIS\n\n\nEl splenius cervicis (tambi\xE9n conocido como
    splenius colli) es un m\xFAsculo en la parte posterior del cuello.\n\nSurge por
    una estrecha banda tendinosa de las ap\xF3fisis espinosas de la tercera a la
    sexta v\xE9rtebra tor\xE1cica; se inserta, por fasc\xEDculos tendinosos, en los
    tub\xE9rculos posteriores de las ap\xF3fisis transversas de las dos o tres v\xE9rtebras
    cervicales superiores.\n\nSu nombre se basa en la palabra griega \u03C3\u03C0\u03BB\u03B7\u03BD\u03AF\u03BF\u03BD,
    splenion (que significa vendaje) y la palabra latina cervix (que significa cuello).
    \n\nLa palabra collum tambi\xE9n se refiere al cuello en lat\xEDn. La funci\xF3n
    del m\xFAsculo splenius cervicis es la extensi\xF3n de la columna cervical, la
    rotaci\xF3n hacia el lado ipsilateral y la flexi\xF3n lateral hacia el lado ipsilateral.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splenius_cervicis_muscle\n\r\n;;;FR;;;\r\n\n\n\nMUSCLE
    SPLENIUS COLLI/CERVICIS\n\n\nLe splenius cervicis (\xE9galement connu sous le
    nom de splenius colli) est un muscle situ\xE9 \xE0 l'arri\xE8re du cou.\n\nIl
    na\xEEt par une \xE9troite bande tendineuse des apophyses \xE9pineuses de la
    troisi\xE8me \xE0 la sixi\xE8me vert\xE8bre thoracique ; il s'ins\xE8re, par
    des faisceaux tendineux, dans les tubercules post\xE9rieurs des apophyses transverses
    des deux ou trois vert\xE8bres cervicales sup\xE9rieures.\n\nSon nom est bas\xE9
    sur le mot grec \u03C3\u03C0\u03BB\u03B7\u03BD\u03AF\u03BF\u03BD, splenion (signifiant
    un bandage) et le mot latin cervix (signifiant un cou).\n\nLe mot collum fait
    \xE9galement r\xE9f\xE9rence au cou en latin. La fonction du muscle spl\xE9nius
    du col de l'ut\xE9rus est l'extension de la colonne cervicale, la rotation vers
    le c\xF4t\xE9 ipsilat\xE9ral et la flexion lat\xE9rale vers le c\xF4t\xE9 ipsilat\xE9ral.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splenius_cervicis_muscle\n\r\n;;;PT;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULO
    ESPL\xCANIO DO COLO/CERVICIS\n\n\nO espl\xEAnio do colo do \xFAtero (tamb\xE9m
    conhecido como espl\xEAnio do colo) \xE9 um m\xFAsculo na parte de tr\xE1s do
    pesco\xE7o.\n\nOrigina-se por uma estreita faixa tend\xEDnea dos processos espinhosos
    da terceira \xE0 sexta v\xE9rtebras tor\xE1cicas; \xE9 inserido, por fasc\xEDculos
    tend\xEDneos, nos tub\xE9rculos posteriores dos processos transversos das duas
    ou tr\xEAs v\xE9rtebras cervicais superiores.\n\nSeu nome \xE9 baseado na palavra
    grega \u03C3\u03C0\u03BB\u03B7\u03BD\u03AF\u03BF\u03BD, splenion (que significa
    curativo) e na palavra latina colo (que significa pesco\xE7o). \n\nA palavra
    collum tamb\xE9m se refere ao pesco\xE7o em latim. A fun\xE7\xE3o do m\xFAsculo
    espl\xEAnio cervical \xE9 extens\xE3o da coluna cervical, rota\xE7\xE3o para
    o lado ipsilateral e flex\xE3o lateral para o lado ipsilateral.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splenius_cervicis_muscle\n"
