  allNames:
  - occipitalis muscle
  - musculus occipitalis
  - muscle occipital
  - "m\xFAsculo occipital"
  - "m\xFAsculo occipital"
  - muscolo occipitale
  - occipitalis spier
  - occipitalis-muskel
  - "mi\u0119sie\u0144 potyliczny"
  - "\u6795\u808C"
  description: "OCCIPITALIS MUSCLE\r\n\r\n\r\nThe occipitalis muscle (occipital belly)
    is a muscle which covers parts of the skull. \r\n\r\nSome sources consider the
    occipital muscle to be a distinct muscle. \r\n\r\nHowever, Terminologia Anatomica
    currently classifies it as part of the occipitofrontalis muscle along with the
    frontalis muscle.\r\n\r\nThe occipitalis muscle is thin and quadrilateral in
    form. \r\n\r\nIt arises from tendinous fibers from the lateral two-thirds of
    the superior nuchal line of the occipital bone and from the mastoid process of
    the temporal and ends in the epicranial aponeurosis.\r\n\r\nThe occipitalis muscle
    is innervated by the facial nerve and its function is to move the scalp back.
    \r\n\r\nThe muscles receives blood from the occipital artery.\r\n\r\n\r\n== Additional
    image ==\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occipitalis_muscle\r\n;;;ES;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULO
    OCCIPITAL\n\n\nEl m\xFAsculo occipital (vientre occipital) es un m\xFAsculo que
    cubre partes del cr\xE1neo. \n\nAlgunas fuentes consideran que el m\xFAsculo
    occipital es un m\xFAsculo distinto.\n\nSin embargo, Terminologia Anatomica actualmente
    lo clasifica como parte del m\xFAsculo occipitofrontal junto con el m\xFAsculo
    frontal.\n\nEl m\xFAsculo occipital es delgado y de forma cuadril\xE1tera.\n\nSurge
    de las fibras tendinosas de los dos tercios laterales de la l\xEDnea nucal superior
    del hueso occipital y de la ap\xF3fisis mastoides del temporal y termina en la
    aponeurosis epicraneana.\n\nEl m\xFAsculo occipital est\xE1 inervado por el nervio
    facial y su funci\xF3n es mover el cuero cabelludo hacia atr\xE1s.\n\nLos m\xFAsculos
    reciben sangre de la arteria occipital.\n\n\n== Imagen adicional ==\n\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occipitalis_muscle\n\r\n;;;FR;;;\r\n\n\n\nMUSCLE
    OCCIPITALIS\n\n\nLe muscle occipital (ventre occipital) est un muscle qui recouvre
    certaines parties du cr\xE2ne. \n\nCertaines sources consid\xE8rent le muscle
    occipital comme un muscle distinct.\n\nCependant, Terminologia Anatomica le classe
    actuellement comme faisant partie du muscle occipitofrontal avec le muscle frontal.\n\nLe
    muscle occipital est mince et de forme quadrilat\xE8re.\n\nIl na\xEEt des fibres
    tendineuses des deux tiers lat\xE9raux de la ligne nucale sup\xE9rieure de l'os
    occipital et de l'apophyse masto\xEFdienne du temporal et se termine par l'apon\xE9vrose
    \xE9picr\xE2nienne.\n\nLe muscle occipital est innerv\xE9 par le nerf facial
    et sa fonction est de faire reculer le cuir chevelu.\n\nLes muscles re\xE7oivent
    le sang de l'art\xE8re occipitale.\n\n\n== Image suppl\xE9mentaire ==\n\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occipitalis_muscle\n\r\n;;;PT;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULO
    OCCIPITALIS\n\n\nO m\xFAsculo occipital (ventre occipital) \xE9 um m\xFAsculo
    que cobre partes do cr\xE2nio.\n\nAlgumas fontes consideram o m\xFAsculo occipital
    um m\xFAsculo distinto.\n\nNo entanto, a Terminologia Anatomica atualmente o
    classifica como parte do m\xFAsculo occipitofrontal junto com o m\xFAsculo frontal.\n\nO
    m\xFAsculo occipital \xE9 fino e quadril\xE1tero na forma.\n\nOrigina-se de fibras
    tend\xEDneas dos dois ter\xE7os laterais da linha nucal superior do osso occipital
    e do processo mast\xF3ide do temporal e termina na aponeurose epicraniana.\n\nO
    m\xFAsculo occipital \xE9 inervado pelo nervo facial e sua fun\xE7\xE3o \xE9
    mover o couro cabeludo para tr\xE1s.\n\nOs m\xFAsculos recebem sangue da art\xE9ria
    occipital.\n\n\n== Imagem adicional ==\n\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occipitalis_muscle\n"
