--- !u!114 &7755606783840635171
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7755606783840635181}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 00fda604ac3af404a8e8a7571f24c19d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  allNames:
  - scapulohumeral muscles
  - musculi scapulohumerales
  - "muscles scapulo-hum\xE9raux"
  - "m\xFAsculos escapulohumerales"
  - "m\xFAsculos escapuloumerais"
  - muscoli scapolo-omerali
  - scapulohumerale spieren
  - schulterblattmuskulatur
  - "mi\u0119\u015Bnie \u0142opatkowo-ramienne"
  - "\u80A9\u80DB\u80B1\u9AA8"
  description: "SCAPULOHUMERAL MUSCLES\r\n\r\n    Posterior:\r\n        Supraspinatus,
    infraspinatus, teres minor, subscapularis, deltoideus, latissimus dorsi, teres
    major\r\n    \r\n    Anterior:\r\n        Pectoralis major, coracobrachialis\r\n\r\nThe
    scapulohumeral muscles are a group of seven muscles that connect the humerus
    to the scapula. \r\n\r\nThey are amongst the muscles that act on and stabilise
    the glenohumeral joint in the human body.\r\n\r\nThey include :\r\n\r\n-coracobrachialis
    muscle\r\n-deltoid muscle\r\n-rotator cuff muscles :infraspinatus muscle\r\n-subscapularis
    muscle\r\n-supraspinatus muscle\r\n-teres minor muscleteres major muscle\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scapulohumeral_muscles\r\n;;;ES;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULOS
    ESCAPULOHUMERALES\n\nPosterior:\nSupraespinoso, infraespinoso, redondo menor,
    subescapular, deltoides, dorsal ancho, redondo mayor\n \nAnterior:\nPectoral
    mayor, coracobraquial\n\nLos m\xFAsculos escapulohumerales son un grupo de siete
    m\xFAsculos que conectan el h\xFAmero con la esc\xE1pula. \n\nSe encuentran entre
    los m\xFAsculos que act\xFAan sobre la articulaci\xF3n glenohumeral y la estabilizan
    en el cuerpo humano.\n\nIncluyen :\n\n-m\xFAsculo coracobraquial\n-musculo deltoide\n-M\xFAsculos
    del manguito rotador: m\xFAsculo infraespinoso\n-m\xFAsculo subescapular\n-m\xFAsculo
    supraespinoso\n-m\xFAsculo redondo menorm\xFAsculo redondo mayor\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scapulohumeral_muscles\n\r\n;;;FR;;;\r\n\n\n\nMUSCLES
    SCAPULOHUM\xC9RAUX\n\n Post\xE9rieur:\n Supraspinatus, infraspinatus, teres minor,
    subscapularis, deltoideus, latissimus dorsi, teres major\n \n Ant\xE9rieur:\n
    Grand pectoral, coracobrachial\n\nLes muscles scapulohum\xE9raux sont un groupe
    de sept muscles qui relient l'hum\xE9rus \xE0 l'omoplate. \n\nIls font partie
    des muscles qui agissent sur et stabilisent l'articulation gl\xE9no-hum\xE9rale
    du corps humain.\n\nIls incluent :\n\n-muscle coracobrachial\n-muscle delto\xEFde\n-muscles
    de la coiffe des rotateurs : muscle sous-\xE9pineux\n-muscle sous-scapulaire\n-muscle
    sus-\xE9pineux\n- muscle petit rond muscle grand rond\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scapulohumeral_muscles\n\r\n;;;PT;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULOS
    ESCAPULO-HUMERAIS\n\n Posterior:\n Supraespinhal, infraespinhal, redondo menor,
    subescapular, deltoideus, latissimus dorsi, redondo maior\n \n Anterior:\n Peitoral
    maior, coracobraquial\n\nOs m\xFAsculos escapuloumerais s\xE3o um grupo de sete
    m\xFAsculos que conectam o \xFAmero \xE0 esc\xE1pula. \n\nEles est\xE3o entre
    os m\xFAsculos que atuam e estabilizam a articula\xE7\xE3o glenoumeral no corpo
    humano.\n\nEles incluem :\n\n- m\xFAsculo coracobraquial\n-m\xFAsculo deltoide\n-
    M\xFAsculos do manguito rotador: m\xFAsculo infraespinhoso\n-m\xFAsculo subescapular\n-
    m\xFAsculo supraespinhal\n- M\xFAsculo redondo menor M\xFAsculo redondo maior\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scapulohumeral_muscles\n"
