--- !u!114 &8244045205188010689
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 8244045205188010691}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 00fda604ac3af404a8e8a7571f24c19d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  allNames:
  - infrahyoid muscles
  - musculi infrahyoidei
  - "muscles infra-hyo\xEFdiens"
  - "m\xFAsculos infrahioideos"
  - "m\xFAsculos infra-hi\xF3ideos"
  - muscoli infraioidei
  - infrahyoid spieren
  - infrahyoideusmuskulatur
  - "mi\u0119\u015Bnie podgnykowe"
  - "\u820C\u4E0B\u808C"
  description: "INFRAHYOID MUSCLES\r\n\r\n\r\nThe infrahyoid muscles, or strap muscles,
    are a group of four pairs of muscles in the anterior (frontal) part of the neck.
    \r\n\r\nThe four infrahyoid muscles are the sternohyoid, sternothyroid, thyrohyoid
    and omohyoid muscles.\r\n\r\nExcluding the sternothyroid, the infrahyoid muscles
    either originate from or insert on to the hyoid bone.\r\n\r\nThe term infrahyoid
    refers to the region below the hyoid bone, while the term strap muscles refers
    to the long and flat muscle shapes which resembles a strap. \r\n\r\nThe stylopharyngeus
    muscle is considered by many to be one of the strap muscles, but is not an infrahyoid
    muscle.\r\n\r\n\r\n== Individual muscles ==\r\n\r\nThe origin, insertion and
    innervation of the individual muscles:\r\n\r\n\r\n=== Nerve supply ===\r\n\r\nAll
    of the infrahyoid muscles are innervated by the ansa cervicalis from the cervical
    plexus (C1-C3) except the thyrohyoid muscle, which is innervated by fibers only
    from the first cervical spinal nerve travelling with the hypoglossal nerve.\r\n\r\n\r\n==
    Function ==\r\n\r\nThe infrahyoid muscles function to elevate and depress the
    hyoid bone and larynx during swallowing and speech. \r\n\r\nThis moves the larynx
    as one unit.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrahyoid_muscles\r\n;;;ES;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULOS
    INFRAHIOIDEOS\n\n\nLos m\xFAsculos infrahioideos, o m\xFAsculos infrahioideos,
    son un grupo de cuatro pares de m\xFAsculos en la parte anterior (frontal) del
    cuello. \n\nLos cuatro m\xFAsculos infrahioideos son los m\xFAsculos esternohioideo,
    esternotiroideo, tirohioideo y omohioideo.\n\nExcluyendo el esternotiroideo,
    los m\xFAsculos infrahioideos se originan o se insertan en el hueso hioides.\n\nEl
    t\xE9rmino infrahioideo se refiere a la regi\xF3n debajo del hueso hioides, mientras
    que el t\xE9rmino m\xFAsculos de la correa se refiere a las formas musculares
    largas y planas que se asemejan a una correa. \n\nMuchos consideran que el m\xFAsculo
    estilofar\xEDngeo es uno de los m\xFAsculos de la correa, pero no es un m\xFAsculo
    infrahioideo.\n\n\n== M\xFAsculos individuales ==\n\nEl origen, inserci\xF3n
    e inervaci\xF3n de los m\xFAsculos individuales:\n\n\n=== Suministro nervioso
    ===\n\nTodos los m\xFAsculos infrahioideos est\xE1n inervados por el asa cervical
    del plexo cervical (C1-C3), excepto el m\xFAsculo tirohioideo, que est\xE1 inervado
    solo por fibras del primer nervio espinal cervical que viajan con el nervio hipogloso.\n\n\n==
    Funci\xF3n ==\n\nLos m\xFAsculos infrahioideos funcionan para elevar y deprimir
    el hueso hioides y la laringe durante la degluci\xF3n y el habla. \n\nEsto mueve
    la laringe como una unidad.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrahyoid_muscles\n\r\n;;;FR;;;\r\n\n\n\nMUSCLES
    SOUS-HYOIDIENS\n\n\nLes muscles infrahyo\xEFdiens, ou muscles de la sangle, sont
    un groupe de quatre paires de muscles dans la partie ant\xE9rieure (frontale)
    du cou.\n\nLes quatre muscles infra-hyo\xEFdiens sont les muscles sterno-hyo\xEFdien,
    sterno-thyro\xEFdien, thyro-hyo\xEFdien et omo-hyo\xEFdien.\n\n\xC0 l'exclusion
    du sternothyro\xEFdien, les muscles infrahyo\xEFdiens proviennent ou s'ins\xE8rent
    sur l'os hyo\xEFde.\n\nLe terme infrahyo\xEFde fait r\xE9f\xE9rence \xE0 la r\xE9gion
    situ\xE9e sous l'os hyo\xEFde, tandis que le terme muscles de la sangle fait
    r\xE9f\xE9rence aux formes musculaires longues et plates qui ressemblent \xE0
    une sangle.\n\nLe muscle stylopharyng\xE9 est consid\xE9r\xE9 par beaucoup comme
    l'un des muscles de la sangle, mais n'est pas un muscle infrahyo\xEFdien.\n\n\n==
    Muscles individuels ==\n\nL'origine, l'insertion et l'innervation des muscles
    individuels\_:\n\n\n=== Innervation ===\n\nTous les muscles sous-hyo\xEFdiens
    sont innerv\xE9s par l'anse cervicale du plexus cervical (C1-C3), \xE0 l'exception
    du muscle thyrohyo\xEFdien, qui est innerv\xE9 uniquement par les fibres du premier
    nerf rachidien cervical voyageant avec le nerf hypoglosse.\n\n\n== Fonction ==\n\nLes
    muscles sous-hyo\xEFdiens ont pour fonction d'\xE9lever et d'abaisser l'os hyo\xEFde
    et le larynx pendant la d\xE9glutition et la parole. \n\nCela d\xE9place le larynx
    comme une unit\xE9.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrahyoid_muscles\n\r\n;;;PT;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULOS
    INFRA-HI\xD3IDES\n\n\nOs m\xFAsculos infra-hi\xF3ideos, ou m\xFAsculos da cinta,
    s\xE3o um grupo de quatro pares de m\xFAsculos na parte anterior (frontal) do
    pesco\xE7o.\n\nOs quatro m\xFAsculos infra-hi\xF3ideos s\xE3o os m\xFAsculos
    esterno-hi\xF3ideo, esternotire\xF3ideo, tireo-hi\xF3ideo e omo-hi\xF3ideo.\n\nExcluindo
    o esternotire\xF3ideo, os m\xFAsculos infra-hi\xF3ideos se originam ou se inserem
    no osso hi\xF3ide.\n\nO termo infra-hi\xF3ideo refere-se \xE0 regi\xE3o abaixo
    do osso hi\xF3ide, enquanto o termo m\xFAsculos da cinta refere-se \xE0s formas
    musculares longas e planas que se assemelham a uma cinta.\n\nO m\xFAsculo estilofar\xEDngeo
    \xE9 considerado por muitos como um dos m\xFAsculos da cinta, mas n\xE3o \xE9
    um m\xFAsculo infra-hi\xF3ideo.\n\n\n== M\xFAsculos individuais ==\n\nA origem,
    inser\xE7\xE3o e inerva\xE7\xE3o dos m\xFAsculos individuais:\n\n\n=== Suprimento
    nervoso ===\n\nTodos os m\xFAsculos infra-hi\xF3ideos s\xE3o inervados pela al\xE7a
    cervical do plexo cervical (C1-C3), exceto o m\xFAsculo tireo-hi\xF3ideo, que
    \xE9 inervado por fibras apenas do primeiro nervo espinhal cervical que viaja
    com o nervo hipoglosso.\n\n\n== Fun\xE7\xE3o ==\n\nOs m\xFAsculos infra-hi\xF3ideos
    funcionam para elevar e abaixar o osso hi\xF3ide e a laringe durante a degluti\xE7\xE3o
    e a fala. \n\nIsso move a laringe como uma unidade.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infrahyoid_muscles\n"
