--- !u!114 &8623410695815598202
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 8623410695815598470}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 00fda604ac3af404a8e8a7571f24c19d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  allNames:
  - opponens digiti minimi muscle of hand
  - musculus opponens digiti minimi manus
  - muscle opposant du petit doigt
  - "oponens digiti minimi m\xFAsculo de la mano"
  - "m\xFAsculo oponente digital m\xEDnimo da m\xE3o"
  - opponens digiti minimi muscolo della mano
  - opponens digiti minimi handspier
  - opponens digiti minimi handmuskel
  - "opponens digiti minimi mi\u0119sie\u0144 r\u0119ki"
  - "\u5C0D\u624B\u5C0F\u6307\u808C"
  description: "OPPONENS DIGITI MINIMI MUSCLE OF HAND\r\n\r\n\r\nThe opponens digiti
    minimi (opponens digiti quinti in older texts) is a muscle in the hand. \r\n\r\nIt
    is of a triangular form, and placed immediately beneath the palmaris brevis,
    abductor digiti minimi and flexor digiti minimi brevis. \r\n\r\nIt is one of
    the three hypothenar muscles that control the little finger.\r\n\r\nIt arises
    from the convexity of the hamulus of the hamate bone and the contiguous portion
    of the transverse carpal ligament; it is inserted into the whole length of the
    metacarpal bone of the little finger, along its ulnar margin.\r\n\r\nThe opponens
    digiti minimi muscle serves to flex and laterally rotate the 5th metacarpal about
    the 5th carpometacarpal joint, as when bringing the little finger and thumb into
    opposition. \r\n\r\nIt is innervated by the deep branch of the ulnar nerve.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opponens_digiti_minimi_muscle_of_hand\r\n;;;ES;;;\r\n\n\n\nOPONENTES
    DIGITI MINIMI M\xDASCULO DE LA MANO\n\n\nEl opponens digiti minimi (opponens
    digiti quinti en textos m\xE1s antiguos) es un m\xFAsculo de la mano.\n\nTiene
    forma triangular y se coloca inmediatamente debajo del palmar corto, el abductor
    digiti minimi y el flexor digiti minimi brevis.\n\nEs uno de los tres m\xFAsculos
    hipotenares que controlan el dedo me\xF1ique.\n\nSurge de la convexidad del hamulus
    del hueso ganchoso y la porci\xF3n contigua del ligamento transverso del carpo;
    se inserta en toda la longitud del hueso metacarpiano del dedo me\xF1ique, a
    lo largo de su margen cubital.\n\nEl m\xFAsculo oponente digiti minimi sirve
    para flexionar y rotar lateralmente el quinto metacarpiano alrededor de la quinta
    articulaci\xF3n carpometacarpiana, como cuando se oponen el dedo me\xF1ique y
    el pulgar. \n\nEst\xE1 inervado por la rama profunda del nervio cubital.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opponens_digiti_minimi_muscle_of_hand\n\r\n;;;FR;;;\r\n\n\n\nADVERSAIRES
    DIGITI MINIMI MUSCLE DE LA MAIN\n\n\nL'opponens digiti minimi (opponens digiti
    quinti dans les textes plus anciens) est un muscle de la main. \n\nIl est de
    forme triangulaire et plac\xE9 imm\xE9diatement sous le palmaris brevis, le abducteur
    digiti minimi et le flexor digiti minimi brevis. \n\nC'est l'un des trois muscles
    hypoth\xE9nar qui contr\xF4lent le petit doigt.\n\nIl provient de la convexit\xE9
    de l'hamulus de l'os hamat\xE9 et de la partie contigu\xEB du ligament carpien
    transverse ; il est ins\xE9r\xE9 dans toute la longueur de l'os m\xE9tacarpien
    du petit doigt, le long de son bord ulnaire.\n\nLe muscle digiti minimi de l'adversaire
    sert \xE0 fl\xE9chir et \xE0 faire pivoter lat\xE9ralement le 5e m\xE9tacarpien
    autour de la 5e articulation carpom\xE9tacarpienne, comme lors de l'opposition
    de l'auriculaire et du pouce. \n\nIl est innerv\xE9 par la branche profonde du
    nerf cubital.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opponens_digiti_minimi_muscle_of_hand\n\r\n;;;PT;;;\r\n\n\n\nM\xDASCULO
    DA M\xC3O OPPONENS DIGITI MINIMI\n\n\nO opponens digiti minimi (opponens digiti
    quinti em textos mais antigos) \xE9 um m\xFAsculo da m\xE3o.\n\n\xC9 de forma
    triangular, e colocado imediatamente abaixo do palmar curto, abdutor do dedo
    m\xEDnimo e flexor do dedo m\xEDnimo.\n\n\xC9 um dos tr\xEAs m\xFAsculos hipotenares
    que controlam o dedo m\xEDnimo.\n\nOrigina-se da convexidade do h\xE2mulo do
    osso hamato e da por\xE7\xE3o cont\xEDgua do ligamento transverso do carpo; \xE9
    inserido em toda a extens\xE3o do osso metacarpal do dedo m\xEDnimo, ao longo
    de sua margem ulnar.\n\nO m\xFAsculo oponente do dedo m\xEDnimo serve para flexionar
    e girar lateralmente o 5\xBA metacarpo em torno da 5\xAA articula\xE7\xE3o carpometacarpal,
    como quando o dedo m\xEDnimo e o polegar se op\xF5em. \n\n\xC9 inervado pelo
    ramo profundo do nervo ulnar.\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opponens_digiti_minimi_muscle_of_hand\n"
