--- !u!114 &8730353499721799999
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 8730353499721799995}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 00fda604ac3af404a8e8a7571f24c19d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  allNames:
  - flexor digitorum superficialis
  - flexor superficialis digitorum superficialis
  - "muscle fl\xE9chisseur superficiel des doigts"
  - flexor superficial de los dedos
  - flexor superficial dos dedos
  - flessore superficiale delle dita
  - flexor digitorum superficialis
  - flexor digitorum superficialis
  - flexor digitorum superficialis
  - "\u8DBE\u6DFA\u5C48\u808C"
  description: "FLEXOR DIGITORUM SUPERFICIALIS (MUSCLE)\r\n\r\n\r\nFlexor digitorum
    superficialis (flexor digitorum sublimis) is an extrinsic flexor muscle of the
    fingers at the proximal interphalangeal joints.\r\n\r\nIt is in the anterior
    compartment of the forearm. \r\n\r\nIt is sometimes considered to be the deepest
    part of the superficial layer of this compartment, and sometimes considered to
    be a distinct, \"intermediate layer\" of this compartment. \r\n\r\nIt is relatively
    common for the Flexor digitorum superficialis to be missing from the little finger,
    bilaterally and unilaterally, which can cause problems when diagnosing a little
    finger injury.\r\n\r\n\r\n== Structure ==\r\n\r\nThe muscle has two classically
    described heads \u2013 the humeroulnar and radial \u2013 and it is between these
    heads that the median nerve and ulnar artery pass. \r\n\r\nThe ulnar collateral
    ligament of elbow joint gives its origin to part of this muscle.\r\n\r\nFour
    long tendons come off this muscle near the wrist and travel through the carpal
    tunnel formed by the flexor retinaculum. \r\n\r\nThese tendons, along with those
    of flexor digitorum profundus, are enclosed by a common flexor sheath. \r\n\r\nThe
    tendons attach to the anterior margins on the bases of the intermediate phalanges
    of the four fingers. \r\n\r\nThese tendons have a split (Camper's Chiasm) at
    the end of them through which the tendons of flexor digitorum profundus pass.\r\n\r\n\r\n===
    Innervation ===\r\n\r\nThe Flexor digitorium superficialis muscle is innervated
    by the median nerve (C7, C8, T1).\r\n\r\n\r\n== Function ==\r\n\r\nThe primary
    function of flexor digitorum superficialis is flexion of the middle phalanges
    of the four fingers (excluding the thumb) at the proximal interphalangeal joints,
    however under continued action it also flexes the metacarpophalangeal joints
    and wrist joint.\r\n\r\nTo test flexor digitorum superficialis, one finger is
    flexed at the proximal interphalangeal joint against resistance, while the remaining
    three fingers are held fully extended (to inactivate flexor digitorum profundus).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flexor_digitorum_superficialis_muscle\r\n;;;ES;;;\r\n\n\n\nFLEXOR
    DIGITORUM SUPERFICIALIS (M\xDASCULO)\n\n\nFlexor digitorum superficialis (flexor
    digitorum sublimis) es un m\xFAsculo flexor extr\xEDnseco de los dedos en las
    articulaciones interfal\xE1ngicas proximales.\n\nEst\xE1 en el compartimento
    anterior del antebrazo. \n\nA veces se considera que es la parte m\xE1s profunda
    de la capa superficial de este compartimento y, a veces, se considera que es
    una \"capa intermedia\" distinta de este compartimento. \n\nEs relativamente
    com\xFAn que falte el Flexor digitorum superficialis del dedo me\xF1ique, bilateral
    y unilateralmente, lo que puede causar problemas al diagnosticar una lesi\xF3n
    en el dedo me\xF1ique.\n\n\n== Estructura ==\n\nEl m\xFAsculo tiene dos cabezas
    descritas cl\xE1sicamente, la humerocubital y la radial, y es entre estas cabezas
    donde pasan el nervio mediano y la arteria cubital. \n\nEl ligamento colateral
    cubital de la articulaci\xF3n del codo da origen a parte de este m\xFAsculo.\n\nCuatro
    largos tendones salen de este m\xFAsculo cerca de la mu\xF1eca y viajan a trav\xE9s
    del t\xFAnel carpiano formado por el retin\xE1culo flexor. \n\nEstos tendones,
    junto con los del flexor digitorum profundus, est\xE1n encerrados por una vaina
    flexora com\xFAn.\n\nLos tendones se unen a los m\xE1rgenes anteriores en las
    bases de las falanges intermedias de los cuatro dedos.\n\nEstos tendones tienen
    una hendidura (quiasma de Camper) al final de ellos a trav\xE9s de los cuales
    pasan los tendones del flexor digitorum profundus.\n\n\n=== Inervaci\xF3n ===\n\nEl
    m\xFAsculo Flexor digitorium superficialis est\xE1 inervado por el nervio mediano
    (C7, C8, T1).\n\n\n== Funci\xF3n ==\n\nLa funci\xF3n principal del flexor digitorum
    superficialis es la flexi\xF3n de las falanges medias de los cuatro dedos (excluyendo
    el pulgar) en las articulaciones interfal\xE1ngicas proximales; sin embargo,
    bajo acci\xF3n continua, tambi\xE9n flexiona las articulaciones metacarpofal\xE1ngicas
    y la articulaci\xF3n de la mu\xF1eca.\n\nPara probar el flexor digitorum superficialis,
    se flexiona un dedo en la articulaci\xF3n interfal\xE1ngica proximal contra resistencia,
    mientras que los tres dedos restantes se mantienen completamente extendidos (para
    inactivar el flexor digitorum profundus).\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flexor_digitorum_superficialis_muscle\n\r\n;;;FR;;;\r\n\n\n\nFLEXOR
    DIGITORUM SUPERFICIALIS (MUSCLE)\n\n\nFlexor digitorum superficialis (flexor
    digitorum sublimis) est un muscle fl\xE9chisseur extrins\xE8que des doigts au
    niveau des articulations interphalangiennes proximales.\n\nC'est dans la loge
    ant\xE9rieure de l'avant-bras. \n\nIl est parfois consid\xE9r\xE9 comme la partie
    la plus profonde de la couche superficielle de ce compartiment, et parfois consid\xE9r\xE9
    comme une \"couche interm\xE9diaire\" distincte de ce compartiment. \n\nIl est
    relativement courant que le Flexor digitorum superficialis soit absent du petit
    doigt, bilat\xE9ralement et unilat\xE9ralement, ce qui peut poser des probl\xE8mes
    lors du diagnostic d'une blessure au petit doigt.\n\n\n== Structure ==\n\nLe
    muscle a deux t\xEAtes classiquement d\xE9crites - l'hum\xE9ro-ulnaire et la
    radiale - et c'est entre ces t\xEAtes que passent le nerf m\xE9dian et l'art\xE8re
    ulnaire. \n\nLe ligament collat\xE9ral ulnaire de l'articulation du coude donne
    son origine \xE0 une partie de ce muscle.\n\nQuatre longs tendons sortent de
    ce muscle pr\xE8s du poignet et traversent le canal carpien form\xE9 par le r\xE9tinaculum
    des fl\xE9chisseurs. \n\nCes tendons, ainsi que ceux du fl\xE9chisseur profond
    des doigts, sont entour\xE9s d'une gaine commune de fl\xE9chisseurs.\n\nLes tendons
    s'attachent aux marges ant\xE9rieures \xE0 la base des phalanges interm\xE9diaires
    des quatre doigts.\n\nCes tendons ont une fente (chiasme de Camper) \xE0 leur
    extr\xE9mit\xE9 \xE0 travers laquelle passent les tendons du fl\xE9chisseur profond
    des doigts.\n\n\n=== Innervation ===\n\nLe muscle Flexor digitorium superficialis
    est innerv\xE9 par le nerf m\xE9dian (C7, C8, T1).\n\n\n== Fonction ==\n\nLa
    fonction principale du fl\xE9chisseur superficiel des doigts est la flexion des
    phalanges m\xE9dianes des quatre doigts (\xE0 l'exclusion du pouce) au niveau
    des articulations interphalangiennes proximales, mais sous une action continue,
    il fl\xE9chit \xE9galement les articulations m\xE9tacarpo-phalangiennes et l'articulation
    du poignet.\n\nPour tester le fl\xE9chisseur superficiel des doigts, un doigt
    est fl\xE9chi au niveau de l'articulation interphalangienne proximale contre
    r\xE9sistance, tandis que les trois doigts restants sont maintenus compl\xE8tement
    \xE9tendus (pour inactiver le fl\xE9chisseur profond des doigts).\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flexor_digitorum_superficialis_muscle\n\r\n;;;PT;;;\r\n\n\n\nFLEXOR
    DIGITORUM SUPERFICIALIS (M\xDASCULO)\n\n\nFlexor digitorum superficialis (flexor
    digitorum sublimis) \xE9 um m\xFAsculo flexor extr\xEDnseco dos dedos nas articula\xE7\xF5es
    interfal\xE2ngicas proximais.\n\nEst\xE1 no compartimento anterior do antebra\xE7o.
    \n\n\xC0s vezes, \xE9 considerada a parte mais profunda da camada superficial
    desse compartimento e, \xE0s vezes, considerada uma \"camada intermedi\xE1ria\"
    distinta desse compartimento. \n\n\xC9 relativamente comum que o flexor superficial
    dos dedos esteja ausente do dedo m\xEDnimo, bilateral e unilateralmente, o que
    pode causar problemas no diagn\xF3stico de uma les\xE3o no dedo m\xEDnimo.\n\n\n==
    Estrutura ==\n\nO m\xFAsculo possui duas cabe\xE7as classicamente descritas \u2013
    a \xFAmeroulnar e a radial \u2013 e \xE9 entre essas cabe\xE7as que passam o
    nervo mediano e a art\xE9ria ulnar. \n\nO ligamento colateral ulnar da articula\xE7\xE3o
    do cotovelo d\xE1 origem a parte deste m\xFAsculo.\n\nQuatro longos tend\xF5es
    saem desse m\xFAsculo pr\xF3ximo ao punho e percorrem o t\xFAnel do carpo formado
    pelo retin\xE1culo dos flexores. \n\nEsses tend\xF5es, juntamente com os do flexor
    profundo dos dedos, s\xE3o envolvidos por uma bainha flexora comum.\n\nOs tend\xF5es
    fixam-se \xE0s margens anteriores nas bases das falanges intermedi\xE1rias dos
    quatro dedos.\n\nEsses tend\xF5es t\xEAm uma divis\xE3o (Quiasma de Camper) na
    extremidade deles, por onde passam os tend\xF5es do flexor profundo dos dedos.\n\n\n===
    Inerva\xE7\xE3o ===\n\nO m\xFAsculo flexor superficial dos dedos \xE9 inervado
    pelo nervo mediano (C7, C8, T1).\n\n\n== Fun\xE7\xE3o ==\n\nA fun\xE7\xE3o prim\xE1ria
    do flexor superficial dos dedos \xE9 a flex\xE3o das falanges m\xE9dias dos quatro
    dedos (excluindo o polegar) nas articula\xE7\xF5es interfal\xE2ngicas proximais,
    no entanto, sob a\xE7\xE3o cont\xEDnua, tamb\xE9m flexiona as articula\xE7\xF5es
    metacarpofal\xE2ngicas e a articula\xE7\xE3o do punho.\n\nPara testar o flexor
    superficial dos dedos, um dedo \xE9 flexionado na articula\xE7\xE3o interfal\xE2ngica
    proximal contra resist\xEAncia, enquanto os tr\xEAs dedos restantes s\xE3o mantidos
    totalmente estendidos (para inativar o flexor profundo dos dedos).\n\n\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flexor_digitorum_superficialis_muscle\n"
